The Salesforce “Ohana” (or family) works together every day to improve the state of the world. Our Aloha culture is built on eight core values that unite us, inspire us, and make us uniquely Salesforce.
We respect and value employees from every background, and we thrive as a result.
We donate 1% of our time, product, and profit to those who need it most: our 1-1-1 model.
We’re obsessed with our customers’ success and take pride in their achievements.
We communicate openly with our customers, and do what it takes to keep their data secure.
We pursue ideas that could change our company, our country — and maybe even the world.
We create public mission statements every year to keep us aligned and accountable.
We take care of ourselves and each other first, so we can do more for our customers.
We work with talented, passionate people. And when we reach our goals, we celebrate.
We donate 1% of our time, product, and profit to those who need it most."
CRM,Salesforce,Technology,2018,salesforce.com/company,1,about page,primary page,20180104004637,https://web.archive.org/web/20180104004637id_/https://www.salesforce.com/company/,ok,,225,"The Fourth Industrial Revolution is changing the way people work, using robotics, AI, the Internet of Things, and more. By making these innovations easier and more accessible, we're helping create a future with greater opportunity and equality for all.
Trailblazers don't fear change, we embrace it. We harness new technologies to entirely transform our companies, our careers, and hopefully, our world.
In Hawaiian culture, “Ohana” means family; it's the tie that binds people together. Our Ohana is built on four core values that inspire us to work together every day toward improving the world.
In 1999, we pioneered CRM software in the cloud, helping 150,000+ companies run their business smarter. Today, we're creating a whole new economy that's helping millions of Salesforce users improve their lives, too.
Everyday, more than 150,000 companies just like yours are increasing employee productivity, team collaboration, customer loyalty and, most importantly, their sales using the world’s #1 CRM platform.
Our innovative cloud-based platform gets accolades from press around the world, but it’s the dedication to helping our customers succeed that's made us the world’s 4th-largest software company.
*From FORTUNE® Magazine, March 15, 2017 © 2017 Time Inc. FORTUNE and 100 Best Companies to Work For are registered trademarks and are used under License. FORTUNE and Time Inc. are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of, Salesforce."
