BAC,Bank of America,Financials,2018,about.bankofamerica.com,1,about page,primary page,20180116181948,https://web.archive.org/web/20180116181948id_/http://about.bankofamerica.com/,ok,,1342,"We're committed to creating a more inclusive world for all of us.
[On screen copy] Support Services at Bank of America employs over 300 people with intellectual disabilities
Music throughout
Selina Waller - So many success stories in here, it’s just crazy.
[On screen copy] Keri Laws, Support Services Employee
Keri Laws - It makes me feel really good that I’m getting married this year.
[On screen copy] Dawn Trinidad, Support Services Employee
Dawn Trinidad - I’m a good influence on my son because I got my job here.
[On screen copy] Selina Waller, Support Services Employee
Selina - Everybody encourage you to do your best.
Dawn - Yes, this is a job that I can do!
Selina - I have a future here.
Keri - We’ve become friends here at Bank of America, it’s like a family.
[On screen copy] Bank of America signage
Kelly Fredrickson - Support Services is an organization within Bank of America of about 300 people with intellectual disabilities. And they do graphic design, printing, kitting, fulfilling, and inventory management.
[On screen copy] Kelly Fredrickson, Creative, Brand and Agency Management Executive
Kelly - That’s what they do. Who they are is one of the best parts of Bank of America.
[On screen copy] Mark Feinour, Support Services Executive
Mark Feinour - The culture within Support Services is for our teammates to look out for each other. And what we found with Ron and Terence is, they have a special relationship. Ron is a great resource for Terence, to help him get to and from the building each morning. And then on the flip side, Terence is a help with Ron when they sit there and do fulfillment jobs together. They compliment each other well with their abilities.
Speaker - Ron is an asset to the team, keep up the great job Ron.
[On screen copy] Anne Finucane, Vice Chairman
Anne Finucane - So much of what you do is about the respect that we’re giving to our customers. Without your help, we simply would not do as well. And you should congratulate yourselves for that.
Mark - We consider Support Services like any other line of business. Everything that we do within Support Services is 100% quality checked. And 99% of our business is repeat business because our customers see what we do and realize that they’re getting a better product at a lower cost than they would using an outside supplier.
Kelly - We have a real opportunity and responsibility at Bank of America to demonstrate inclusivity, to demonstrate what it means to build a diverse workforce, to demonstrate that we understand our customers’ needs, all of our customers. And I think having a group like Support Services integral to the fabric of Bank of America helps all of our employees understand what it means to work in an inclusive place.
Selina - Hey guys, how we doing this morning?
(laughter)
Selina - Family, and I mean it from the bottom of my heart. This is family. From the moment we come in the morning till the time we leave, this is us.
